           'New Pretty Town supplies its young residents with food, housing and entertainment without ordinary wage purchase. Apartment wall systems manufacture many requested goods from raw inputs. This establishes a continuing technologically supported cohort, rather than a single wealthy teenager. The strong guarantee estimate applies within that status-defined group; entry depends on the compulsory operation, and it is not a promise of equal freedom or the same support outside the city.\n\nControl remains concentrated in human city institutions, including the authorities that enforce surgery and suppress resistance. Asking a wall for an item does not give the recipient ownership of its supply. Young New Pretties are mainly described as enjoying parties and recreation, while later Middle Pretties take occupations. That supports a high, broadly uncertain nonworking estimate for the young cohort only. Useful creative activity and exceptional responsibilities still count as work, so the estimate is not a literal statement that everyone does nothing. The later political transformation and its new resource pressures are covered separately.',
